# Mobile session

Send `X-Client-Type: mobile` on login, refresh, and logout. Store the access token and the refresh token only in `flutter_secure_storage`. The refresh token travels in the JSON body. Do not use cookies, and do not log either token.

Register sends `fullName`, `phone`, `email`, and `password`. The account can log in before email verification. Activate and reset send `phone` or `code` plus `password`. Confirm password stays on the device.

A `MASTER_ADMIN` or `SYSTEM_ADMIN` session is cleared and stays on login. This app is for `STUDENT`.

```dart
// BAD — refresh token in preferences or a cookie jar
prefs.setString('refreshToken', body['refreshToken']);

// GOOD — secure storage, body on the next refresh
await secure.write(key: 'refreshToken', value: body['refreshToken'] as String);
